INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Aries', 'Your deepest wound is around your own identity and right to exist as you are. You''ve learned that being authentically yourself is dangerous, that your natural assertiveness makes you too much. The wound asks: Can I be myself without apology? Can I trust my own impulses?', 'You struggle to initiate. Even when you know what you want, something inside stops you from going after it. You may come across as hesitant or uncertain when inside you''re burning with desire. You''re prone to starting strong then second-guessing yourself mid-stride.', 'You attract people who need your courage more than you trust your own. You may find yourself in relationships where you''re the passive one, waiting to be chosen. Your partners often sense your doubt before you do, and it becomes a dynamic you play out together.', 'The hardest part is the constant self-doubt that shadows your impulses. You can''t tell if you''re being wise or cowardly. There''s also deep frustration—you see others charge forward and wonder why you can''t, which breeds resentment at yourself and them.', 'Your healing comes through reclaiming small acts of courage. Start with what you secretly want and do it, even imperfectly. Your wound becomes your gift when you guide others in trusting their own impulses, when you show them it''s possible to be yourself without destroying everything.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Taurus', 'Your deepest wound is about your fundamental worth—whether you deserve good things, comfort, stability, and real resources. You learned early that self-worth was conditional, that you had to earn the right to exist safely. The question haunts you: Am I enough just as I am?', 'You may oscillate between self-deprivation and desperation. You push away luxury or comfort with one hand while craving security with the other. Money, your body, and material well-being become battlegrounds. You''re either depriving yourself to prove your worthiness or overindulging to numb the emptiness.', 'You attract people who either overvalue or devalue you—rarely the healthy middle. You may settle for relationships where you''re not truly treasured, or you push away partners who genuinely care. Your insecurity about your worth contaminates the intimacy; you can''t fully believe you''re loved.', 'The deepest pain is the constant internal poverty despite external abundance. You may have resources but never feel secure. Your body becomes a source of shame and self-judgment. There''s also the exhaustion of constantly trying to prove your value rather than simply living it.', 'Healing happens when you begin offering yourself the tenderness you''d give a beloved. Your wound transforms into the ability to help others reclaim their worth, to see value in the overlooked and underestimated. You become a healer of shame, someone who teaches others they''re already enough.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Gemini', 'Your deepest wound is around being heard and understood. You learned that your voice doesn''t matter, that what you think is less important than what others believe. Your mind is sharp but burdened by the belief that intelligence isn''t enough to make you valuable. Can anyone truly understand you?', 'You talk without being listened to, or you stay silent even when you have something crucial to say. You may become a chronic explainer, desperate to make yourself clear, or retreat into cold logic to avoid the vulnerability of real communication. Your thoughts scatter when you need them most.', 'You often feel fundamentally misunderstood in relationships, even with people who care. You attract partners who listen superficially or dismiss your perspective. You struggle to have real conversations—either over-explaining or shutting down. Intimacy requires being known, and you''re terrified you never can be.', 'The hardest part is the loneliness of being surrounded by people yet unheard. You question your own intelligence constantly, second-guessing what you know. There''s also deep anxiety about saying the wrong thing, being perceived as stupid, or being exposed as a fraud who doesn''t actually know anything.', 'Your healing comes through finding your actual voice—not explaining yourself to be understood, but speaking your truth to those who are listening. Your wound becomes your greatest gift when you help others find their voice too, when you truly hear them in a way no one heard you.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Cancer', 'Your deepest wound is about belonging and safety—about having a true home, whether physical or emotional. You needed nurturing and either received it conditionally or not at all. You''ve spent your life searching for someone or somewhere that feels like home. Does anywhere truly welcome you as you are?', 'You fluctuate between clinginess and withdrawal, between needing reassurance and pushing people away. You may struggle to leave unhealthy situations (jobs, relationships, families) because the familiar feels safer than the unknown. Or you don''t stay anywhere long enough to build the safety you crave, always searching.', 'You magnetize either caretakers or people who need caretaking—rarely equals. You struggle to let yourself be vulnerable without losing yourself. Emotional intimacy triggers your deepest fears about rejection and abandonment. You may mother others while secretly wanting to be mothered, creating imbalanced dynamics.', 'The deepest pain is homesickness that no place can cure. You''re caught between deep loyalty to origins that hurt you and desperate longing for something better. There''s also guilt—you want to take care of others, but you''re exhausted from not being cared for yourself.', 'Healing comes through recognizing that home isn''t a place, it''s a feeling you create inside yourself. Your wound transforms into the ability to provide real emotional safety for others—not the suffocating kind, but genuine holding space. You become a healer of family wounds, someone who helps others belong to themselves first.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Leo', 'Your deepest wound is about creative self-expression and being truly seen. You learned that shining made you a target, that your light threatens others. Part of you wants desperately to be witnessed; another part hides what makes you unique. Can you be visible without becoming vulnerable to judgment?', 'You either perform constantly, seeking validation, or you hide your gifts entirely. You may feel like a fraud whenever you receive praise, convinced people don''t see the "real" you. There''s a gap between your inner sense of significance and your external expression of it—and you''re ashamed of both.', 'You attract relationships where your creative self is either idolized or dismissed. You struggle to share yourself authentically without either diminishing yourself or making it all about you. There''s a deep fear that if someone really knew your creative desires, they''d leave. Intimacy requires exposure you''re terrified to give.', 'The hardest part is the constant self-judgment about your creative expression. You may have enormous talent but underutilize it out of fear. There''s also resentment—you see others celebrated for far less, which triggers both desire and despair about your own worthiness of attention.', 'Your healing comes through creating not for applause but for the truth it contains. Your wound becomes your gift when you help others find their voice and creative courage, when you witness others'' brilliance the way you secretly wish to be witnessed yourself.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Virgo', 'Your deepest wound is perfectionism coupled with a fear that you''re fundamentally inadequate. You learned that your value comes from what you do, not who you are. You''re hypercritical of yourself while also deeply sensitive to criticism. The question torments you: Will I ever be good enough?', 'You''re driven by impossible standards—in your work, your body, your routines, your mind. You notice every flaw first, in yourself and others. You''re prone to exhaustion from constant self-improvement efforts. Your body often reflects your inner anxiety: tension, digestive issues, nervous system dysregulation from the relentless pressure you place on yourself.', 'You attract relationships where you''re the one doing all the managing and maintenance, or you retreat into judgment when others don''t meet your standards. You struggle to be imperfect with someone, to let them see your flaws and still be loved. Intimacy requires accepting yourself as is, which feels impossible.', 'The deepest pain is knowing you''ll never meet your own standards. You''re enslaved to improvement and still feel broken. There''s also deep loneliness—you''re so focused on fixing yourself that you never fully inhabit your own life. And the exhaustion is relentless; you don''t know how to rest without feeling lazy.', 'Healing comes through accepting "good enough" as genuinely good. Your wound transforms when you redirect your analytical gifts toward helping others stop the self-sabotage. You become a healer of perfectionism, someone who teaches people to work with their bodies instead of against them, to be useful without being used up.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Libra', 'Your deepest wound is about relationships themselves—about your worth in the eyes of others and your need to be chosen. You learned that partnership and approval are essential, but also dangerous. You sacrifice yourself to maintain connection, terrified of abandonment. Can you be loved while being yourself?', 'You seek balance by disappearing. You''re so attuned to others'' needs that you lose yourself in relationships. You struggle to make decisions independently, always checking them against others'' preferences. You may jump from relationship to relationship because being alone feels unbearable, even when the relationship itself isn''t healthy.', 'You attract people who need you to disappear—they thrive on your attentiveness. Genuine reciprocity is hard to find because you''ve trained yourself to be the accommodating one. You resent your partners for not noticing your sacrifice, even though you never asked them to. Intimacy becomes a game of codependency rather than true meeting.', 'The hardest part is losing yourself so completely that you don''t know who you are outside of a relationship. There''s rage underneath all your pleasantness—rage at the compromises you''ve made, rage at not being truly chosen. You also fear that if you stopped being accommodating, no one would stay.', 'Healing comes through learning that being yourself is not a threat to relationships—it''s the foundation. Your wound becomes your gift when you help others stop abandoning themselves for love, when you teach that true partnership requires both people to be fully present.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Scorpio', 'Your deepest wound is about trust, power, and vulnerability. You learned early that closeness brings pain, that revealing yourself invites betrayal. You''re drawn to intensity yet terrified by it. The central question haunts you: If I let someone truly know me, will they destroy me?', 'You oscillate between extremes—complete walls or total fusion with someone, nothing in between. You''re hypervigilant about others'' intentions, scanning for betrayal. You may become obsessed with power dynamics, trying to control situations so you can''t be hurt. Secrecy feels like safety; transparency feels like suicide.', 'You attract relationships with high drama and intensity, often mirroring your inner landscape of extremes. Real intimacy—the kind that requires being seen without armor—feels almost impossible. You may sabotage good relationships before others can leave you. Or you stay in harmful situations because at least the betrayal is familiar.', 'The deepest pain is the loneliness of being profoundly isolated while craving profound connection. You''re aware of emotional undercurrents others miss, which makes you both powerful and paranoid. There''s also the exhaustion of constantly strategizing, of never truly relaxing because trust feels reckless.', 'Healing comes through learning that vulnerability is power, not weakness. Your wound becomes your gift when you help others navigate their own darkness safely—not by pretending it doesn''t exist, but by witnessing it without judgment. You become a healer of the unbearable, someone who can sit with what others fear to name.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Sagittarius', 'Your deepest wound is about meaning, truth, and freedom. You''ve experienced profound disillusionment—beliefs shattered, truths revealed as lies, freedom restricted by circumstances. You''re a seeker forever chasing answers that satisfy. The wound asks: Can I trust anything? Can I ever truly be free?', 'You may swing between rigid dogmatism and cynical nihilism, searching for certainty in a world that provides none. You explore endlessly—philosophies, religions, travels—hoping to find the answer that makes everything make sense. You can be restless, unable to commit to any one path. Or you grasp tightly to beliefs as protection against chaos.', 'You attract people who share your search or who want to ground your wandering. You struggle with commitment in relationships because deep down you fear being trapped by someone else''s truth. You may inadvertently abandon partners in your quest for meaning, or sabotage good things because they feel too limiting.', 'The hardest part is the longing for certainty in a fundamentally uncertain world. You''ve glimpsed the limits of every belief system, which makes faith terrifying. There''s also the exhaustion of constant questioning, and the loneliness of having seen through illusions others still hold dear.', 'Healing comes through accepting that meaning isn''t found—it''s created. Your wound becomes your gift when you help others develop their own wisdom rather than imposing yours, when you inspire genuine seeking instead of blind belief. You become a guide through disillusionment, someone who teaches that freedom and belonging can coexist.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Capricorn', 'Your deepest wound is about authority, power, and legacy. You learned that love is conditional on achievement, that you must earn your right to exist. You carry responsibility that wasn''t yours to carry. The wound haunts you: Am I only valued for what I produce? Can I ever truly be safe?', 'You work relentlessly, driven by fear of failure and irrelevance. You may seem controlled and composed on the surface while internally terrified of being exposed as inadequate. You struggle to rest, to play, to be soft—these feel frivolous or dangerous. Your body may carry years of tension from this constant vigilance.', 'You attract people who need you to be strong and capable—you become the one others depend on. But you can''t let yourself depend on anyone; that would be weakness. You struggle with authority figures because you''re still fighting old battles about whether you''re allowed to succeed, whether you''re truly worthy of power.', 'The deepest pain is feeling ancient—you''ve carried weight since childhood. There''s deep doubt about whether anything you build will matter, whether you''ll ever feel truly secure. There''s also rage at the unfairness of having to grow up so fast, at the childhood you had to forfeit.', 'Healing comes through recognizing that you''re allowed to matter without producing anything. Your wound transforms when you use your hard-won wisdom to help others carry their burdens with more grace. You become a healer of shame around vulnerability, teaching that strength includes knowing when to let others hold you.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Aquarius', 'Your deepest wound is about belonging—fitting in without disappearing, being yourself without being exiled. You''ve always been the outsider, the odd one, the misfit. Part of you rebels against belonging; part of you desperately wants to be chosen. The wound asks: Is there anywhere I truly fit?', 'You may oscillate between isolation and forced belonging, between your radical truth and exhausting conformity. You can feel alienated even in groups, observing from the outside. You''re brilliant at detaching from emotion to stay safe, but this leaves you profoundly lonely. You might seek approval from unusual places or deliberately distance yourself before others can reject you.', 'You attract people who appreciate your uniqueness but also find you hard to reach. You struggle with genuine vulnerability because it threatens your independence—your defenses. You fear that real intimacy will require you to be normal, to shrink yourself, to betray your authentic vision. Connection feels impossible at your truth level.', 'The hardest part is the loneliness of being wired differently. You see the world differently and often can''t share that without being seen as broken or cold. There''s also grief—you''ve sacrificed genuine closeness to protect your individuality, and you''re not sure it was worth it.', 'Healing comes through understanding that your differentness is not a flaw to overcome but a gift to integrate. Your wound becomes your greatest asset when you help others embrace what makes them strange, when you create genuine community for people who don''t fit anywhere else. You become a healer of isolation, showing that belonging doesn''t require erasing yourself.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
INSERT INTO kb_planet_in_sign (planet, sign, summary, life_patterns, relationships, challenges, growth, book_references) VALUES
('Chiron', 'Pisces', 'Your deepest wound is about boundaries and spiritual pain—absorbing everyone else''s suffering as if it''s yours. You''re porous, intuitive, and terrified of the darkness you can feel everywhere. You learned that escape was survival. The wound asks: How do I help without drowning? Can I feel everything without falling apart?', 'You merge with others'' emotions so completely that you don''t know where they end and you begin. You may be drawn to addictive patterns—substances, relationships, spirituality—as ways to escape the unbearable empathic weight you carry. Your body holds everyone else''s pain before it holds your own. You oscillate between saviorism and victimhood.', 'You attract people who need healing and see you as a spiritual fix. Real mutuality is nearly impossible because you''re always reading others'' needs and adjusting yourself. You struggle to know what you actually feel versus what you''re picking up from others. Intimacy requires boundaries you''re not sure you''re allowed to have.', 'The deepest pain is spiritual exhaustion—you feel the weight of collective suffering and question why existence must hurt so much. You''re prone to despair when faced with the world''s pain. There''s also the terror of being alone with your own feelings without escape, without someone else to focus on, without substances or spirituality to numb you.', 'Healing comes through learning that compassion requires boundaries, not dissolution. Your wound becomes your greatest power when you help others safely process their pain without becoming entangled in it. You become a healer of spiritual wounds, teaching that feeling deeply doesn''t require losing yourself, that salvation doesn''t require self-sacrifice.', ARRAY['Reinhart, Chiron and the Healing Journey']);
